# Versions

`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` in `apps/web/package.json`. The footer shows it. Tag `vX.Y.Z` on `main` only when shipping. See `docs/releases.mdx`.

Start at `0.1.0`. `1.0.0` means stable. The existing tag `v1.0.0` is the first demo — leave it, and do not bump from `1.0.x`. Read the current number from `package.json`.

| Change | Bump | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Fix, copy, style | Patch | `0.1.1` |
| Feature | Minor | `0.2.0` |
| Break, while major is 0 | Minor | `0.2.0` |
| Stable product, or a break after `1.0.0` | Major | `1.0.0` |

Release notes use the same shape every time. Write them by hand:

```md
## Summary

- One to three bullets.

**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/vitalvie/vital/compare/vPREV...vNEXT
```
